From 389abd21df317895f3ecdc20e141f5f8b672748d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spencer Bryngelson <sbryngelson@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:15:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [flang][OpenMP] Gate the allocate clause at OpenMP 5.0

`allocate` is an OpenMP 5.0 clause, but 58 of the 62 directives that allow it
declared it as bare `VersionedClause<OMPC_Allocate>`. `VersionedClause` defaults
to `min = 1`, so those 58 accepted the clause at every version. Only `do`,
`taskgroup`, `parallel do` (50) and `scope` (52) were gated.

flang defaults to OpenMP 3.1, so an invocation with no `-fopenmp-version=` lands
in the ungated range: semantics accepts the clause, `ConstructDecomposition`
then correctly refuses to decompose it, and lowering consumes the empty result
and crashes. With the gate it is a diagnostic instead.

This fixes reachability only. Consuming a failed decomposition reads
uninitialized memory, and that path is unchanged here.

Nine tests exercised `allocate` through bare `%openmp_flags` and so depended on
the missing gate. Seven get `-fopenmp-version=50`; the two `allocators` tests
get 52, matching the OpenMP version their own header comments document.

Part of #211430.
